    "description": "A place in Lower Egypt on the eastern bank of the Nile River, mentioned in the Antonine Itinerary. Possibly located in the vicinity of Bubastis.",
    "details": "<p>According to G. Beer (RE: Vicus Iudaeorum), the place should be distinguished from Castra Iudaeorum mentioned in Notitia Dignitatum. In Trismegistos, however, the two are considered the same place. </p>",
